IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc8-part8-maid.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 241.1 to 241.4 (Medical Assistance in Dying).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc8-part7-houses.l4 (JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING).
-- This module is imported by ccc8-part8-homicide (s 227), ccc8-part8-organs-suicide (s 241) and ccc8-part8-harm (s 245), which take their definitions from section 241.1.
-- The core `Party` has no "medical practitioner", "nurse practitioner", "pharmacist" or "Minister of Health": local party types are declared under the section label (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- The information, form, manner, time and recipient of the filing under section 241.31 are set by regulations outside the sources: they enter as facts, and no deadline is invented.

§ `Section 241.1 -- Definitions`

-- src:4645 | medical assistance in dying means
-- src:4646 | (a) the administering by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner of a substance to a person, at their request, that causes their death; or
-- src:4647 | (b) the prescribing or providing by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner of a substance to a person, at their request, so that they may self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death. (aide médicale à mourir)
@ref s 241.1 medical assistance in dying (src:4645-4647)
GIVEN `a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner administers a substance to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administering is at their request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the substance causes their death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner prescribes or provides a substance to a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribing or providing is at their request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is so that they may self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.1 medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    IF     (`a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner administers a substance to a person` AND `the administering is at their request` AND `the substance causes their death`)
        OR (`a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner prescribes or provides a substance to a person` AND `the prescribing or providing is at their request` AND `it is so that they may self-administer the substance and in doing so cause their own death`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "medical assistance in dying means (a) the administering by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner of a substance to a person, at their request, that causes their death; or (b) the prescribing or providing"

-- src:4648 | medical practitioner means a person who is entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province. (médecin)
@ref s 241.1 medical practitioner (src:4648-4648)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.1 medical practitioner` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "medical practitioner means a person who is entitled to practise medicine under the laws of a province"

-- src:4649 | nurse practitioner means a registered nurse who, under the laws of a province, is entitled to practise as a nurse practitioner — or under an equivalent designation — and to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients. (infirmier praticien)
@ref s 241.1 nurse practitioner (src:4649-4649)
GIVEN `the person is a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the laws of a province the nurse is entitled to practise as a nurse practitioner, or under an equivalent designation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nurse is entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.1 nurse practitioner` MEANS
    IF `the person is a registered nurse` AND `under the laws of a province the nurse is entitled to practise as a nurse practitioner, or under an equivalent designation` AND `the nurse is entitled to autonomously make diagnoses, order and interpret diagnostic tests, prescribe substances and treat patients`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nurse practitioner means a registered nurse who, under the laws of a province, is entitled to practise as a nurse practitioner"

-- src:4650 | pharmacist means a person who is entitled to practise pharmacy under the laws of a province. (pharmacien)
@ref s 241.1 pharmacist (src:4650-4650)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to practise pharmacy under the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.1 pharmacist` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to practise pharmacy under the laws of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "pharmacist means a person who is entitled to practise pharmacy under the laws of a province"

§ `Section 241.2 -- Eligibility for medical assistance in dying`

-- src:4665 | (2.1) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(a), a mental illness is not considered to be an illness, disease or disability.
@ref s 241.2(2.1) (src:4665-4665)
GIVEN `the illness, disease or disability relied on is a mental illness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(2.1) a mental illness is not considered to be an illness, disease or disability` MEANS
    IF `the illness, disease or disability relied on is a mental illness`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a mental illness is not considered to be an illness, disease or disability"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says only what a mental illness is not considered to be

-- src:4659 | (2) A person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition only if they meet all of the following criteria:
-- src:4660 | (a) they have a serious and incurable illness, disease or disability;
-- src:4661 | (b) they are in an advanced state of irreversible decline in capability; and
-- src:4662 | (c) that illness, disease or disability or that state of decline causes them enduring physical or psychological suffering that is intolerable to them and that cannot be relieved under conditions that they consider acceptable.
@ref s 241.2(2) (grievous and irremediable medical condition) (src:4659-4662)
GIVEN `they have a serious and incurable illness, disease or disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a mental illness is not considered to be an illness, disease or disability, by s 241.2(2.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `they are in an advanced state of irreversible decline in capability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that illness, disease or disability or that state of decline causes them enduring physical or psychological suffering that is intolerable to them and that cannot be relieved under conditions that they consider acceptable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(2) the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition` MEANS
    IF     `they have a serious and incurable illness, disease or disability`
       AND (NOT (`a mental illness is not considered to be an illness, disease or disability, by s 241.2(2.1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
       AND `they are in an advanced state of irreversible decline in capability`
       AND `that illness, disease or disability or that state of decline causes them enduring physical or psychological suffering that is intolerable to them and that cannot be relieved under conditions that they consider acceptable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition only if they meet all of the following criteria"

-- src:4652 | 241.2 (1) A person may receive medical assistance in dying only if they meet all of the following criteria:
-- src:4653 | (a) they are eligible — or, but for any applicable minimum period of residence or waiting period, would be eligible — for health services funded by a government in Canada;
-- src:4654 | (b) they are at least 18 years of age and capable of making decisions with respect to their health;
-- src:4655 | (c) they have a grievous and irremediable medical condition;
-- src:4656 | (d) they have made a voluntary request for medical assistance in dying that, in particular, was not made as a result of external pressure; and
-- src:4657 | (e) they give informed consent to receive medical assistance in dying after having been informed of the means that are available to relieve their suffering, including palliative care.
@ref s 241.2(1) (src:4652-4657)
GIVEN `they are eligible, or but for any applicable minimum period of residence or waiting period would be eligible, for health services funded by a government in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `their age, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `they are capable of making decisions with respect to their health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have a grievous and irremediable medical condition, by s 241.2(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `they have made a voluntary request for medical assistance in dying that was not made as a result of external pressure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they give informed consent to receive medical assistance in dying after having been informed of the means that are available to relieve their suffering, including palliative care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(1) the person meets all of the criteria` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the criteria other than (c) are met` AND `they have a grievous and irremediable medical condition, by s 241.2(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the criteria other than (c) are met` AND `they have a grievous and irremediable medical condition, by s 241.2(2)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of subsection (2) is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may receive medical assistance in dying only if they meet all of the following criteria"
    WHERE
        `the criteria other than (c) are met` MEANS
                `they are eligible, or but for any applicable minimum period of residence or waiting period would be eligible, for health services funded by a government in Canada`
            AND `their age, in years` AT LEAST 18
            AND `they are capable of making decisions with respect to their health`
            AND `they have made a voluntary request for medical assistance in dying that was not made as a result of external pressure`
            AND `they give informed consent to receive medical assistance in dying after having been informed of the means that are available to relieve their suffering, including palliative care`

@ref s 241.2(1) (src:4652-4657)
GIVEN `they meet all of the criteria, by s 241.2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(1) the person may receive medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    IF `they meet all of the criteria, by s 241.2(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may receive medical assistance in dying only if they meet all of the following criteria"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if" states a necessary condition; the safeguards of subsections (3) and (3.1) are further conditions on the practitioner

-- src:4696 | (3.2) For the purposes of subsection (3), the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner may administer a substance to a person to cause their death without meeting the requirement set out in paragraph (3)(h) if
-- src:4697 | (a) before the person loses the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying,
-- src:4698 | (i) they met all of the criteria set out in subsection (1) and all other safeguards set out in subsection (3) were met,
-- src:4699 | (ii) they entered into an arrangement in writing with the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner would administer a substance to cause their death on a specified day,
-- src:4700 | (iii) they were informed by the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner of the risk of losing the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying prior to the day specified in the arrangement, and
-- src:4701 | (iv) in the written arrangement, they consented to the administration by the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner of a substance to cause their death on or before the day specified in the arrangement if they lost their capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying prior to that day;
-- src:4702 | (b) the person has lost the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying;
-- src:4703 | (c) the person does not demonstrate, by words, sounds or gestures, refusal to have the substance administered or resistance to its administration; and
-- src:4704 | (d) the substance is administered to the person in accordance with the terms of the arrangement.
@ref s 241.2(3.2) (src:4696-4704)
GIVEN `before the person lost the capacity to consent, they met all of the criteria set out in subsection (1) and all other safeguards set out in subsection (3) were met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before then, they entered into an arrangement in writing with the practitioner that the practitioner would administer a substance to cause their death on a specified day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before then, they were informed by the practitioner of the risk of losing the capacity to consent prior to the day specified in the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the written arrangement, they consented to the administration of a substance to cause their death on or before the day specified if they lost their capacity to consent prior to that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has lost the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes words, sounds or gestures that show refusal to have the substance administered or resistance to its administration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those words, sounds or gestures are involuntary and made in response to contact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the substance is administered to the person in accordance with the terms of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3.2) the practitioner may administer a substance without meeting the requirement of paragraph (3)(h)` MEANS
    IF     `before the person lost the capacity to consent, they met all of the criteria set out in subsection (1) and all other safeguards set out in subsection (3) were met`
       AND `before then, they entered into an arrangement in writing with the practitioner that the practitioner would administer a substance to cause their death on a specified day`
       AND `before then, they were informed by the practitioner of the risk of losing the capacity to consent prior to the day specified in the arrangement`
       AND `in the written arrangement, they consented to the administration of a substance to cause their death on or before the day specified if they lost their capacity to consent prior to that day`
       AND `the person has lost the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying`
       AND (NOT (`the person makes words, sounds or gestures that show refusal to have the substance administered or resistance to its administration` AND (NOT `those words, sounds or gestures are involuntary and made in response to contact`)))
       AND `the substance is administered to the person in accordance with the terms of the arrangement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without meeting the requirement set out in paragraph (3)(h) if (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... and (d) ..." (a failed "if" on a power: the exception is not made and paragraph (3)(h) stays a requirement, so NOTHING, not JUST FALSE, because the function is named for a power: fork F13)

-- src:4706 | (3.3) For greater certainty, involuntary words, sounds or gestures made in response to contact do not constitute a demonstration of refusal or resistance for the purposes of paragraph (3.2)(c).
@ref s 241.2(3.3) (src:4706-4706)
GIVEN `the words, sounds or gestures are involuntary and made in response to contact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3.3) the words, sounds or gestures constitute a demonstration of refusal or resistance` MEANS
    IF `the words, sounds or gestures are involuntary and made in response to contact`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "involuntary words, sounds or gestures made in response to contact do not constitute a demonstration of refusal or resistance"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text says only that involuntary responses to contact are not a demonstration

-- src:4708 | (3.4) Once a person demonstrates, by words, sounds or gestures, in accordance with subsection (3.2), refusal to have the substance administered or resistance to its administration, medical assistance in dying can no longer be provided to them on the basis of the consent given by them under subparagraph (3.2)(a)(iv).
@ref s 241.2(3.4) (src:4708-4708)
GIVEN `the person has demonstrated, by words, sounds or gestures, in accordance with subsection (3.2), refusal to have the substance administered or resistance to its administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3.4) medical assistance in dying can be provided on the basis of the consent given under subparagraph (3.2)(a)(iv)` MEANS
    IF `the person has demonstrated, by words, sounds or gestures, in accordance with subsection (3.2), refusal to have the substance administered or resistance to its administration`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "medical assistance in dying can no longer be provided to them on the basis of the consent given by them under subparagraph (3.2)(a)(iv)"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Once a person demonstrates ... refusal ... or resistance" (the text says nothing of the case before it)

-- src:4710 | (3.5) In the case of a person who loses the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying after self-administering a substance, provided to them under this section, so as to cause their own death, a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner may administer a substance to cause the death of that person if
-- src:4711 | (a) before the person loses the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying, they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner entered into an arrangement in writing providing that the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner would
-- src:4712 | (i) be present at the time the person self-administered the first substance, and
-- src:4713 | (ii) administer a second substance to cause the person’s death if, after self-administering the first substance, the person lost the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying and did not die within a specified period;
-- src:4714 | (b) the person self-administers the first substance, does not die within the period specified in the arrangement and loses the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying; and
-- src:4715 | (c) the second substance is administered to the person in accordance with the terms of the arrangement.
@ref s 241.2(3.5) (src:4710-4715)
GIVEN `the person loses the capacity to consent after self-administering a substance, provided to them under section 241.2, so as to cause their own death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before then, they and the practitioner entered into an arrangement in writing providing that the practitioner would be present at the time the person self-administered the first substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that arrangement provided that the practitioner would administer a second substance to cause the person's death if, after self-administering the first substance, the person lost the capacity to consent and did not die within a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person self-administers the first substance, does not die within the period specified in the arrangement and loses the capacity to consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second substance is administered to the person in accordance with the terms of the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3.5) the practitioner may administer a substance to cause the death of that person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person loses the capacity to consent after self-administering a substance, provided to them under section 241.2, so as to cause their own death`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a person who loses the capacity to consent to receiving medical assistance in dying after self-administering a substance, provided to them under this section, so as to cause their own death" (an "in the case of" condition, the equivalent of "where": marginal reading M2; listed and not flipped, fork F14)
        IF     `the person loses the capacity to consent after self-administering a substance, provided to them under section 241.2, so as to cause their own death`
           AND `before then, they and the practitioner entered into an arrangement in writing providing that the practitioner would be present at the time the person self-administered the first substance`
           AND `that arrangement provided that the practitioner would administer a second substance to cause the person's death if, after self-administering the first substance, the person lost the capacity to consent and did not die within a specified period`
           AND `the person self-administers the first substance, does not die within the period specified in the arrangement and loses the capacity to consent`
           AND `the second substance is administered to the person in accordance with the terms of the arrangement`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner may administer a substance to cause the death of that person if (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..." (a failed "if" on a power, so NOTHING, not JUST FALSE, because the function is named for a power: fork F14)

-- src:4667 | (3) Subject to subsection (3.2), before a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner provides medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is reasonably foreseeable, taking into account all of their medical circumstances, without a prognosis necessarily having been made as to the specific length of time that they have remaining, the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must
-- src:4668 | (a) be of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4669 | (b) ensure that the person’s request for medical assist­ance in dying was
-- src:4670 | (i) made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4), and
-- src:4671 | (ii) signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition;
-- src:4672 | (c) be satisfied that the request was signed and dated by the person — or by another person under subsection (4) — before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request;
-- src:4673 | (d) ensure that the person has been informed that they may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request;
-- src:4674 | (e) ensure that another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4675 | (f) be satisfied that they and the other medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are independent;
-- src:4676 | (g) if the person has difficulty communicating, take all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision; and
-- src:4677 | (h) immediately before providing the medical assist­ance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensure that the person gives express consent to receive medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.2(3) (src:4667-4677)
-- Fork F7: "must (a) ... (h)" is a duty of the practitioner; the function answers whether the requirements HAVE BEEN MET, and answers JUST FALSE when one is not (a bare "must" not done).
GIVEN `the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3)(a) the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria` MEANS
    IF `the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must (a) be of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1)"

-- src:4669 | (b) ensure that the person’s request for medical assist­ance in dying was
-- src:4670 | (i) made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4), and
-- src:4671 | (ii) signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition;
-- src:4672 | (c) be satisfied that the request was signed and dated by the person — or by another person under subsection (4) — before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request;
-- src:4673 | (d) ensure that the person has been informed that they may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request;
-- src:4674 | (e) ensure that another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4675 | (f) be satisfied that they and the other medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are independent;
-- src:4676 | (g) if the person has difficulty communicating, take all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision; and
-- src:4677 | (h) immediately before providing the medical assist­ance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensure that the person gives express consent to receive medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.2(3)(b) to (h) (src:4669-4677)
GIVEN `the request was made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner is satisfied that the request was signed and dated before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been informed that they may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner is satisfied that they and the other practitioner are independent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has difficulty communicating` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner has taken all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, the practitioner gave the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensured that the person gave express consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement of paragraph (h) is waived, by s 241.2(3.2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3)(b) to (h) the requirements have been met` MEANS
    IF     `the request was made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4)`
       AND `it was signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition`
       AND `the practitioner is satisfied that the request was signed and dated before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request`
       AND `the person has been informed that they may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request`
       AND `another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1)`
       AND `the practitioner is satisfied that they and the other practitioner are independent`
       AND ((NOT `the person has difficulty communicating`) OR `the practitioner has taken all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision`)
       AND (   `immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, the practitioner gave the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensured that the person gave express consent`
            OR `the requirement of paragraph (h) is waived, by s 241.2(3.2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must ... (b) ensure ... (c) be satisfied ... (d) ensure ... (e) ensure ... (f) be satisfied ... (g) ... take all necessary measures ... and (h) immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request" (a bare "must" not done: fork F7)

-- src:4667 | (3) Subject to subsection (3.2), before a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner provides medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is reasonably foreseeable, taking into account all of their medical circumstances, without a prognosis necessarily having been made as to the specific length of time that they have remaining, the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must
-- src:4668 | (a) be of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4669 | (b) ensure that the person’s request for medical assist­ance in dying was
-- src:4670 | (i) made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4), and
-- src:4671 | (ii) signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition;
-- src:4672 | (c) be satisfied that the request was signed and dated by the person — or by another person under subsection (4) — before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request;
-- src:4673 | (d) ensure that the person has been informed that they may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request;
-- src:4674 | (e) ensure that another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4675 | (f) be satisfied that they and the other medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are independent;
-- src:4676 | (g) if the person has difficulty communicating, take all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision; and
-- src:4677 | (h) immediately before providing the medical assist­ance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensure that the person gives express consent to receive medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.2(3) (src:4667-4677)
GIVEN `the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria, by s 241.2(3)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of paragraphs (b) to (h) have been met, by s 241.2(3)(b) to (h)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3) the practitioner has met the safeguards before providing medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is reasonably foreseeable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria, by s 241.2(3)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the requirements of paragraphs (b) to (h) have been met, by s 241.2(3)(b) to (h)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "before a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner provides medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is reasonably foreseeable ... the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must" (fork F7)
        IF `the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria, by s 241.2(3)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the requirements of paragraphs (b) to (h) have been met, by s 241.2(3)(b) to (h)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an answer taken from paragraph (a) or paragraphs (b) to (h) is itself not covered

-- src:4692 | (i) ensure that there are at least 90 clear days between the day on which the first assessment under this subsection of whether the person meets the criteria set out in subsection (1) begins and the day on which medical assistance in dying is provided to them or — if the assessments have been completed and they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are both of the opinion that the loss of the person’s capacity to provide consent to receive medical assistance in dying is imminent — any shorter period that the first medical practitioner or nurse practitioner considers appropriate in the circumstances;
@ref s 241.2(3.1)(i) (src:4692-4692)
-- Fork F9: "at least 90 clear days between the day on which the first assessment begins and the day on which medical assistance in dying is provided": clear days exclude both end days,
-- so the days between are the difference of the dates less one.
GIVEN `the day on which the first assessment begins` IS A DATE
      `the day on which medical assistance in dying is provided` IS A DATE
      `the assessments have been completed and both practitioners are of the opinion that the loss of the person's capacity to provide consent is imminent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any shorter period the first practitioner considers appropriate in the circumstances, in clear days (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3.1)(i) there are at least 90 clear days between the first assessment and the day medical assistance in dying is provided` MEANS
    IF `clear days` AT LEAST 90 OR (`the assessments have been completed and both practitioners are of the opinion that the loss of the person's capacity to provide consent is imminent` AND `clear days` AT LEAST `any shorter period the first practitioner considers appropriate in the circumstances, in clear days (0 if none)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ensure that there are at least 90 clear days between the day on which the first assessment ... begins and the day on which medical assistance in dying is provided to them" (a period the text fixes in its own words)
    WHERE
        `clear days` MEANS (Day `the day on which medical assistance in dying is provided` MINUS Day `the day on which the first assessment begins`) MINUS 1

-- src:4682 | (b) ensure that the person’s request for medical assistance in dying was
-- src:4683 | (i) made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4), and
-- src:4684 | (ii) signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition;
-- src:4685 | (c) be satisfied that the request was signed and dated by the person — or by another person under subsection (4) — before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request;
-- src:4686 | (d) ensure that the person has been informed that the person may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request;
-- src:4687 | (e) ensure that another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4688 | (e.1) if neither they nor the other medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) has expertise in the condition that is causing the person’s suffering, ensure that they or the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) consult with a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who has that expertise and share the results of that consultation with the other practitioner;
-- src:4689 | (f) be satisfied that they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are independent;
-- src:4690 | (g) ensure that the person has been informed of the means available to relieve their suffering, including, where appropriate, counselling services, mental health and disability support services, community services and palliative care and has been offered consultations with relevant professionals who provide those services or that care;
-- src:4691 | (h) ensure that they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) have discussed with the person the reasonable and available means to relieve the person’s suffering and they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) agree with the person that the person has given serious consideration to those means;
-- src:4692 | (i) ensure that there are at least 90 clear days between the day on which the first assessment under this subsection of whether the person meets the criteria set out in subsection (1) begins and the day on which medical assistance in dying is provided to them or — if the assessments have been completed and they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are both of the opinion that the loss of the person’s capacity to provide consent to receive medical assistance in dying is imminent — any shorter period that the first medical practitioner or nurse practitioner considers appropriate in the circumstances;
-- src:4693 | (j) if the person has difficulty communicating, take all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision; and
-- src:4694 | (k) immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensure that the person gives express consent to receive medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k) (src:4682-4694)
GIVEN `the request was made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner is satisfied that the request was signed and dated before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been informed that the person may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `neither practitioner has expertise in the condition that is causing the person's suffering` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they or the other practitioner have consulted with a practitioner who has that expertise and shared the results of that consultation with the other practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner is satisfied that they and the other practitioner are independent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been informed of the means available to relieve their suffering, including, where appropriate, counselling services, mental health and disability support services, community services and palliative care and has been offered consultations with relevant professionals who provide those services or that care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioners have discussed with the person the reasonable and available means to relieve the person's suffering and agree with the person that the person has given serious consideration to those means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are at least 90 clear days between the first assessment and the day medical assistance in dying is provided, by s 241.2(3.1)(i)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has difficulty communicating` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner has taken all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, the practitioner gave the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensured that the person gave express consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k) the requirements have been met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the other requirements are met` AND `there are at least 90 clear days between the first assessment and the day medical assistance in dying is provided, by s 241.2(3.1)(i)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the other requirements are met` AND `there are at least 90 clear days between the first assessment and the day medical assistance in dying is provided, by s 241.2(3.1)(i)` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of paragraph (i) is itself not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must ... (b) ... (k) immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request" (a bare "must" not done: fork F7)
    WHERE
        `the other requirements are met` MEANS
                `the request was made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4)`
            AND `it was signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition`
            AND `the practitioner is satisfied that the request was signed and dated before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request`
            AND `the person has been informed that the person may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request`
            AND `another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1)`
            AND ((NOT `neither practitioner has expertise in the condition that is causing the person's suffering`) OR `they or the other practitioner have consulted with a practitioner who has that expertise and shared the results of that consultation with the other practitioner`)
            AND `the practitioner is satisfied that they and the other practitioner are independent`
            AND `the person has been informed of the means available to relieve their suffering, including, where appropriate, counselling services, mental health and disability support services, community services and palliative care and has been offered consultations with relevant professionals who provide those services or that care`
            AND `the practitioners have discussed with the person the reasonable and available means to relieve the person's suffering and agree with the person that the person has given serious consideration to those means`
            AND ((NOT `the person has difficulty communicating`) OR `the practitioner has taken all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision`)
            AND `immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, the practitioner gave the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensured that the person gave express consent`

-- src:4680 | (3.1) Before a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner provides medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is not reasonably foreseeable, taking into account all of their medical circumstances, the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must
-- src:4681 | (a) be of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4682 | (b) ensure that the person’s request for medical assistance in dying was
-- src:4683 | (i) made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4), and
-- src:4684 | (ii) signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition;
-- src:4685 | (c) be satisfied that the request was signed and dated by the person — or by another person under subsection (4) — before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request;
-- src:4686 | (d) ensure that the person has been informed that the person may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request;
-- src:4687 | (e) ensure that another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4688 | (e.1) if neither they nor the other medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) has expertise in the condition that is causing the person’s suffering, ensure that they or the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) consult with a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who has that expertise and share the results of that consultation with the other practitioner;
-- src:4689 | (f) be satisfied that they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are independent;
-- src:4690 | (g) ensure that the person has been informed of the means available to relieve their suffering, including, where appropriate, counselling services, mental health and disability support services, community services and palliative care and has been offered consultations with relevant professionals who provide those services or that care;
-- src:4691 | (h) ensure that they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) have discussed with the person the reasonable and available means to relieve the person’s suffering and they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) agree with the person that the person has given serious consideration to those means;
-- src:4692 | (i) ensure that there are at least 90 clear days between the day on which the first assessment under this subsection of whether the person meets the criteria set out in subsection (1) begins and the day on which medical assistance in dying is provided to them or — if the assessments have been completed and they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are both of the opinion that the loss of the person’s capacity to provide consent to receive medical assistance in dying is imminent — any shorter period that the first medical practitioner or nurse practitioner considers appropriate in the circumstances;
-- src:4693 | (j) if the person has difficulty communicating, take all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision; and
-- src:4694 | (k) immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensure that the person gives express consent to receive medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.2(3.1) (src:4680-4694)
GIVEN `the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria, by s 241.2(3)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of paragraphs (b) to (k) have been met, by s 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(3.1) the practitioner has met the safeguards before providing medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is not reasonably foreseeable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria, by s 241.2(3)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `the requirements of paragraphs (b) to (k) have been met, by s 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Before a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner provides medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is not reasonably foreseeable ... the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must" (fork F7)
        IF `the practitioner is of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria, by s 241.2(3)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the requirements of paragraphs (b) to (k) have been met, by s 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an answer taken from paragraph (a) or paragraphs (b) to (k) is itself not covered

DECLARE `s 241.2 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner`

DECLARE `s 241.2 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 241.2(3) meet the safeguards of paragraphs (a) to (h) before providing medical assistance in dying`
    `s 241.2(3.1) meet the safeguards of paragraphs (a) to (k) before providing medical assistance in dying`
    `s 241.2(7) provide medical assistance in dying with reasonable knowledge, care and skill and in accordance with applicable provincial laws, rules or standards`
    `s 241.2(8) inform the pharmacist, before any pharmacist dispenses the substance, that the substance is intended for medical assistance in dying`

-- src:4667 | (3) Subject to subsection (3.2), before a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner provides medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is reasonably foreseeable, taking into account all of their medical circumstances, without a prognosis necessarily having been made as to the specific length of time that they have remaining, the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must
-- src:4668 | (a) be of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4669 | (b) ensure that the person’s request for medical assist­ance in dying was
-- src:4670 | (i) made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4), and
-- src:4671 | (ii) signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition;
-- src:4672 | (c) be satisfied that the request was signed and dated by the person — or by another person under subsection (4) — before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request;
-- src:4673 | (d) ensure that the person has been informed that they may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request;
-- src:4674 | (e) ensure that another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4675 | (f) be satisfied that they and the other medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are independent;
-- src:4676 | (g) if the person has difficulty communicating, take all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision; and
-- src:4677 | (h) immediately before providing the medical assist­ance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensure that the person gives express consent to receive medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.2(3) (src:4667-4677)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 241.2 party` `s 241.2 act`
`s 241.2(3) the duty to meet the safeguards where natural death is reasonably foreseeable` MEANS
    PARTY `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner`
    MUST `s 241.2(3) meet the safeguards of paragraphs (a) to (h) before providing medical assistance in dying`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` BECAUSE "s 241.2(3): the safeguards were not met before medical assistance in dying was provided"

-- src:4680 | (3.1) Before a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner provides medical assistance in dying to a person whose natural death is not reasonably foreseeable, taking into account all of their medical circumstances, the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner must
-- src:4681 | (a) be of the opinion that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4682 | (b) ensure that the person’s request for medical assistance in dying was
-- src:4683 | (i) made in writing and signed and dated by the person or by another person under subsection (4), and
-- src:4684 | (ii) signed and dated after the person was informed by a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner that the person has a grievous and irremediable medical condition;
-- src:4685 | (c) be satisfied that the request was signed and dated by the person — or by another person under subsection (4) — before an independent witness who then also signed and dated the request;
-- src:4686 | (d) ensure that the person has been informed that the person may, at any time and in any manner, withdraw their request;
-- src:4687 | (e) ensure that another medical practitioner or nurse practitioner has provided a written opinion confirming that the person meets all of the criteria set out in subsection (1);
-- src:4688 | (e.1) if neither they nor the other medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) has expertise in the condition that is causing the person’s suffering, ensure that they or the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) consult with a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who has that expertise and share the results of that consultation with the other practitioner;
-- src:4689 | (f) be satisfied that they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are independent;
-- src:4690 | (g) ensure that the person has been informed of the means available to relieve their suffering, including, where appropriate, counselling services, mental health and disability support services, community services and palliative care and has been offered consultations with relevant professionals who provide those services or that care;
-- src:4691 | (h) ensure that they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) have discussed with the person the reasonable and available means to relieve the person’s suffering and they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) agree with the person that the person has given serious consideration to those means;
-- src:4692 | (i) ensure that there are at least 90 clear days between the day on which the first assessment under this subsection of whether the person meets the criteria set out in subsection (1) begins and the day on which medical assistance in dying is provided to them or — if the assessments have been completed and they and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner referred to in paragraph (e) are both of the opinion that the loss of the person’s capacity to provide consent to receive medical assistance in dying is imminent — any shorter period that the first medical practitioner or nurse practitioner considers appropriate in the circumstances;
-- src:4693 | (j) if the person has difficulty communicating, take all necessary measures to provide a reliable means by which the person may understand the information that is provided to them and communicate their decision; and
-- src:4694 | (k) immediately before providing the medical assistance in dying, give the person an opportunity to withdraw their request and ensure that the person gives express consent to receive medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.2(3.1) (src:4680-4694)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 241.2 party` `s 241.2 act`
`s 241.2(3.1) the duty to meet the safeguards where natural death is not reasonably foreseeable` MEANS
    PARTY `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner`
    MUST `s 241.2(3.1) meet the safeguards of paragraphs (a) to (k) before providing medical assistance in dying`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` BECAUSE "s 241.2(3.1): the safeguards were not met before medical assistance in dying was provided"

-- src:4717 | (4) If the person requesting medical assistance in dying is unable to sign and date the request, another person — who is at least 18 years of age, who understands the nature of the request for medical assistance in dying and who does not know or believe that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person’s death — may do so in the person’s presence, on the person’s behalf and under the person’s express direction.
@ref s 241.2(4) (src:4717-4717)
GIVEN `the person requesting medical assistance in dying is unable to sign and date the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person's age, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the other person understands the nature of the request for medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person knows or believes that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person does so in the person's presence, on the person's behalf and under the person's express direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(4) the other person may sign and date the request on the person's behalf` MEANS
    IF     `the person requesting medical assistance in dying is unable to sign and date the request`
       AND `the other person's age, in years` AT LEAST 18
       AND `the other person understands the nature of the request for medical assistance in dying`
       AND (NOT `the other person knows or believes that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person's death`)
       AND `the other person does so in the person's presence, on the person's behalf and under the person's express direction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the person requesting medical assistance in dying is unable to sign and date the request, another person — who is at least 18 years of age, who understands ..., and who does not know or believe ... — may do so"

-- src:4725 | (5.1) Despite paragraphs (5)(c) and (d), a person who provides health care services or personal care as their primary occupation and who is paid to provide that care to the person requesting medical assistance in dying is permitted to act as an independent witness, except for
-- src:4726 | (a) the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who will provide medical assistance in dying to the person; and
-- src:4727 | (b) the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provided an opinion under paragraph (3)(e) or (3.1)(e), as the case may be, in respect of the person.
@ref s 241.2(5.1) (src:4725-4727)
GIVEN `the person provides health care services or personal care as their primary occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is paid to provide that care to the person requesting medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who will provide medical assistance in dying to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provided an opinion under paragraph (3)(e) or (3.1)(e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(5.1) the person is permitted to act as an independent witness despite paragraphs (5)(c) and (d)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person provides health care services or personal care as their primary occupation` AND `the person is paid to provide that care to the person requesting medical assistance in dying` AND (`the person is the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who will provide medical assistance in dying to the person` OR `the person is the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provided an opinion under paragraph (3)(e) or (3.1)(e)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is permitted to act as an independent witness, except for (a) the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who will provide medical assistance in dying to the person; and (b) the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provided an opinion"
        IF `the person provides health care services or personal care as their primary occupation` AND `the person is paid to provide that care to the person requesting medical assistance in dying`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who provides health care services or personal care as their primary occupation and who is paid to provide that care"

-- src:4719 | (5) Any person who is at least 18 years of age and who understands the nature of the request for medical assist­ance in dying may act as an independent witness, except if they
-- src:4720 | (a) know or believe that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person’s death;
-- src:4721 | (b) are an owner or operator of any health care facility at which the person making the request is being treated or any facility in which that person resides;
-- src:4722 | (c) are directly involved in providing health care serv­ices to the person making the request; or
-- src:4723 | (d) directly provide personal care to the person making the request.
@ref s 241.2(5) (src:4719-4723)
GIVEN `the person's age, in years` IS A NUMBER
      `the person understands the nature of the request for medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows or believes that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person's death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an owner or operator of any health care facility at which the person making the request is being treated or any facility in which that person resides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is directly involved in providing health care services to the person making the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person directly provides personal care to the person making the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is permitted despite paragraphs (5)(c) and (d), by s 241.2(5.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(5) the person may act as an independent witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person's age, in years` BELOW 18 OR (NOT `the person understands the nature of the request for medical assistance in dying`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who is at least 18 years of age and who understands the nature of the request ... may act as an independent witness"
        IF `the person knows or believes that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person's death` OR `the person is an owner or operator of any health care facility at which the person making the request is being treated or any facility in which that person resides`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may act as an independent witness, except if they (a) know or believe that they are a beneficiary ... (b) are an owner or operator of any health care facility"
        IF (`the person is directly involved in providing health care services to the person making the request` OR `the person directly provides personal care to the person making the request`) AND (NOT (`the person is permitted despite paragraphs (5)(c) and (d), by s 241.2(5.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except if they ... (c) are directly involved in providing health care services ...; or (d) directly provide personal care to the person making the request" (unless subsection (5.1) permits)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:4729 | (6) The medical practitioner or nurse practitioner providing medical assistance in dying and the medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who provides the opinion referred to in paragraph (3)(e) or (3.1)(e) are independent if they
-- src:4730 | (a) are not a mentor to the other practitioner or responsible for supervising their work;
-- src:4731 | (b) do not know or believe that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person’s death, other than standard compensation for their services relating to the request; and
-- src:4732 | (c) do not know or believe that they are connected to the other practitioner or to the person making the request in any other way that would affect their objectivity.
@ref s 241.2(6) (src:4729-4732)
GIVEN `they are not a mentor to the other practitioner or responsible for supervising their work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they do not know or believe that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person's death, other than standard compensation for their services relating to the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they do not know or believe that they are connected to the other practitioner or to the person making the request in any other way that would affect their objectivity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(6) the two practitioners are independent` MEANS
    IF `they are not a mentor to the other practitioner or responsible for supervising their work` AND `they do not know or believe that they are a beneficiary under the will of the person making the request, or a recipient, in any other way, of a financial or other material benefit resulting from that person's death, other than standard compensation for their services relating to the request` AND `they do not know or believe that they are connected to the other practitioner or to the person making the request in any other way that would affect their objectivity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are independent if they (a) are not a mentor ... (b) do not know or believe ... and (c) do not know or believe" (an "if" condition: marginal reading M2)

-- src:4734 | (7) Medical assistance in dying must be provided with reasonable knowledge, care and skill and in accordance with any applicable provincial laws, rules or standards.
@ref s 241.2(7) (src:4734-4734)
GIVEN `medical assistance in dying has been provided with reasonable knowledge, care and skill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been provided in accordance with any applicable provincial laws, rules or standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(7) medical assistance in dying has been provided as this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `medical assistance in dying has been provided with reasonable knowledge, care and skill` AND `it has been provided in accordance with any applicable provincial laws, rules or standards`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Medical assistance in dying must be provided with reasonable knowledge, care and skill and in accordance with any applicable provincial laws, rules or standards" (a bare "must" not done: fork F7)

@ref s 241.2(7) (src:4734-4734)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 241.2 party` `s 241.2 act`
`s 241.2(7) the duty to provide medical assistance in dying with reasonable knowledge, care and skill` MEANS
    PARTY `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner`
    MUST `s 241.2(7) provide medical assistance in dying with reasonable knowledge, care and skill and in accordance with applicable provincial laws, rules or standards`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` BECAUSE "s 241.2(7): medical assistance in dying was not provided with reasonable knowledge, care and skill and in accordance with applicable provincial laws, rules or standards"

-- src:4736 | (8) The medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who, in providing medical assistance in dying, prescribes or obtains a substance for that purpose must, before any pharmacist dispenses the substance, inform the pharmacist that the substance is intended for that purpose.
@ref s 241.2(8) (src:4736-4736)
GIVEN `the practitioner, in providing medical assistance in dying, prescribes or obtains a substance for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner informed the pharmacist that the substance is intended for that purpose before any pharmacist dispensed the substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(8) the practitioner has informed the pharmacist` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the practitioner, in providing medical assistance in dying, prescribes or obtains a substance for that purpose` AND `the practitioner informed the pharmacist that the substance is intended for that purpose before any pharmacist dispensed the substance` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the practitioner, in providing medical assistance in dying, prescribes or obtains a substance for that purpose` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before any pharmacist dispenses the substance, inform the pharmacist that the substance is intended for that purpose" (a bare "must" not done: fork F7)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who, in providing medical assistance in dying, prescribes or obtains a substance for that purpose"

@ref s 241.2(8) (src:4736-4736)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 241.2 party` `s 241.2 act`
`s 241.2(8) the duty to inform the pharmacist` MEANS
    PARTY `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner`
    MUST `s 241.2(8) inform the pharmacist, before any pharmacist dispenses the substance, that the substance is intended for medical assistance in dying`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 241.2 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner` BECAUSE "s 241.2(8): the pharmacist was not informed before dispensing that the substance is intended for medical assistance in dying"

-- src:4738 | (9) For greater certainty, nothing in this section compels an individual to provide or assist in providing medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.2(9) (src:4738-4738)
GIVEN `the individual is asked to provide or assist in providing medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.2(9) section 241.2 compels the individual to provide or assist in providing medical assistance in dying` MEANS
    IF `the individual is asked to provide or assist in providing medical assistance in dying`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section compels an individual to provide or assist in providing medical assistance in dying"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the individual has not been asked

§ `Section 241.3 -- Failure to comply with safeguards`

-- src:4740 | 241.3 A medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who, in providing medical assistance in dying, knowingly fails to comply, subject to subsection 241.2(3.2), with all of the requirements set out in paragraphs 241.2(3)(b) to (h) or paragraphs 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k), as the case may be, and with subsection 241.2(8) is guilty of
-- src:4741 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:4742 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 241.3 (src:4740-4742)
-- Fork F8: "knowingly fails to comply ... with all of the requirements set out in paragraphs (3)(b) to (h) ... and with subsection (8)" is read as failing to comply with any of the requirements; the other reading requires failure to comply with every one of them.
GIVEN `the practitioner, in providing medical assistance in dying, knowingly fails to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's natural death is reasonably foreseeable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of paragraphs (3)(b) to (h) have been met, subject to subsection (3.2), by s 241.2(3)(b) to (h)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of paragraphs (3.1)(b) to (k) have been met, by s 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the practitioner has informed the pharmacist, by s 241.2(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.3 the practitioner commits the offence of failing to comply with the safeguards` MEANS
    IF     `the practitioner, in providing medical assistance in dying, knowingly fails to comply`
       AND (   (`the person's natural death is reasonably foreseeable` AND `the requirements of paragraphs (3)(b) to (h) have been met, subject to subsection (3.2), by s 241.2(3)(b) to (h)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            OR ((NOT `the person's natural death is reasonably foreseeable`) AND `the requirements of paragraphs (3.1)(b) to (k) have been met, by s 241.2(3.1)(b) to (k)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            OR `the practitioner has informed the pharmacist, by s 241.2(8)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who, in providing medical assistance in dying, knowingly fails to comply ... is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 241.3 (src:4740-4742)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 241.3 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 241.3(a) (src:4741-4741)
`s 241.3(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 241.3 (src:4740-4742)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 241.3 the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 241.3(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 241.31 -- Filing information`

DECLARE `s 241.31 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 241.31 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who assesses or receives a request`
    `s 241.31 a person responsible for preliminary assessments`
    `s 241.31 a pharmacist or pharmacy technician who dispenses a substance`

DECLARE `s 241.31 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 241.31 provide the information required by the regulations to the recipient designated in them`

-- src:4744 | 241.31 (1) Unless they are exempted under regulations made under subsection (3), a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who carries out an assessment of whether a person meets the criteria set out in subsection 241.2(1) or who receives a written request for medical assistance in dying must, in accordance with those regulations, provide the information required by those regulations to the recipient designated in those regulations.
@ref s 241.31(1) (src:4744-4744)
GIVEN `the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner, by s 241.1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person carries out an assessment of whether a person meets the criteria set out in subsection 241.2(1) or receives a written request for medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.31(1) the practitioner must provide the information required by the regulations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless they are exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)"
        IF `the person is a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner, by s 241.1` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the person carries out an assessment of whether a person meets the criteria set out in subsection 241.2(1) or receives a written request for medical assistance in dying` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who carries out an assessment ... or who receives a written request"

@ref s 241.31(1) (src:4744-4744)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 241.31 party` `s 241.31 act`
`s 241.31(1) the duty of the practitioner to provide the information` MEANS
    PARTY `s 241.31 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who assesses or receives a request`
    MUST `s 241.31 provide the information required by the regulations to the recipient designated in them`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 241.31 a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who assesses or receives a request` BECAUSE "s 241.31(1): the information required by the regulations was not provided to the designated recipient"

-- src:4746 | (1.1) Unless they are exempted under regulations made under subsection (3), any person who has the responsibility to carry out preliminary assessments of whether a person meets the criteria set out in subsection 241.2(1) must, in accordance with those regulations, provide the information required by those regulations to the recipient designated in those regulations.
@ref s 241.31(1.1) (src:4746-4746)
GIVEN `the person has the responsibility to carry out preliminary assessments of whether a person meets the criteria set out in subsection 241.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.31(1.1) the person responsible for preliminary assessments must provide the information required by the regulations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless they are exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)"
        IF `the person has the responsibility to carry out preliminary assessments of whether a person meets the criteria set out in subsection 241.2(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person who has the responsibility to carry out preliminary assessments"

@ref s 241.31(1.1) (src:4746-4746)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 241.31 party` `s 241.31 act`
`s 241.31(1.1) the duty of the person responsible for preliminary assessments to provide the information` MEANS
    PARTY `s 241.31 a person responsible for preliminary assessments`
    MUST `s 241.31 provide the information required by the regulations to the recipient designated in them`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 241.31 a person responsible for preliminary assessments` BECAUSE "s 241.31(1.1): the information required by the regulations was not provided to the designated recipient"

-- src:4748 | (2) Unless they are exempted under regulations made under subsection (3), a pharmacist who dispenses a substance in connection with the provision of medical assistance in dying, or the person permitted to act as a pharmacy technician under the laws of a province who dispenses a substance to aid a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner in providing a person with medical assistance in dying, must, in accordance with those regulations, provide the information required by those regulations to the recipient designated in those regulations.
@ref s 241.31(2) (src:4748-4748)
GIVEN `the person is a pharmacist who dispenses a substance in connection with the provision of medical assistance in dying, or a person permitted to act as a pharmacy technician under the laws of a province who dispenses a substance to aid a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner in providing a person with medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.31(2) the pharmacist or pharmacy technician must provide the information required by the regulations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless they are exempted under regulations made under subsection (3)"
        IF `the person is a pharmacist who dispenses a substance in connection with the provision of medical assistance in dying, or a person permitted to act as a pharmacy technician under the laws of a province who dispenses a substance to aid a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner in providing a person with medical assistance in dying` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a pharmacist who dispenses a substance in connection with the provision of medical assistance in dying, or the person permitted to act as a pharmacy technician"

@ref s 241.31(2) (src:4748-4748)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 241.31 party` `s 241.31 act`
`s 241.31(2) the duty of the pharmacist or pharmacy technician to provide the information` MEANS
    PARTY `s 241.31 a pharmacist or pharmacy technician who dispenses a substance`
    MUST `s 241.31 provide the information required by the regulations to the recipient designated in them`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 241.31 a pharmacist or pharmacy technician who dispenses a substance` BECAUSE "s 241.31(2): the information required by the regulations was not provided to the designated recipient"

-- src:4766 | (4) A medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who knowingly fails to comply with subsection (1), a person having the responsibility to carry out preliminary assessments who knowingly fails to comply with subsection (1.1) or a pharmacist or pharmacy technician who knowingly fails to comply with subsection (2),
-- src:4767 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to a term of imprisonment of not more than two years; or
-- src:4768 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 241.31(4) (src:4766-4768)
DECLARE `s 241.31(4) role` IS ONE OF
    `s 241.31(4) a medical practitioner or nurse practitioner who fails to comply with subsection (1)`
    `s 241.31(4) a person having the responsibility to carry out preliminary assessments who fails to comply with subsection (1.1)`
    `s 241.31(4) a pharmacist or pharmacy technician who fails to comply with subsection (2)`

@ref s 241.31(4) (src:4766-4768)
GIVEN role IS A `s 241.31(4) role`
      `the person knowingly fails to comply with the subsection that applies to them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.31(4) the person commits the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly fails to comply with the subsection that applies to them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who knowingly fails to comply with subsection (1) ... (1.1) ... (2), (a) is guilty of" (marginal reading M1)

@ref s 241.31(4) (src:4766-4768)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 241.31(4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 241.31(4)(a) (src:4767-4767)
`s 241.31(4)(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 241.31(4) (src:4766-4768)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 241.31(4) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 241.31(4)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4770 | (5) Everyone who knowingly contravenes the regulations made under subsection (3)
