§ `Section 241.4 -- Forgery and destruction of documents`

-- src:4788 | (4) In subsection (2), document has the same meaning as in section 321.
@ref s 241.4(4) (src:4788-4788)
GIVEN `it is a document, by s 321 the thing is a document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.4(4) document` MEANS `it is a document, by s 321 the thing is a document`   -- the same answer as section 321 gives: JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING as that section answers

-- src:4776 | 241.4 (1) Everyone commits an offence who commits forgery in relation to a request for medical assistance in dying.
@ref s 241.4(1) (src:4776-4776)
GIVEN `the person commits forgery, by s 366 the person commits forgery` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the forgery is in relation to a request for medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.4(1) the person commits the offence of forgery in relation to a request` MEANS
    IF `the person commits forgery, by s 366 the person commits forgery` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the forgery is in relation to a request for medical assistance in dying`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone commits an offence who commits forgery in relation to a request for medical assistance in dying" (marginal reading M1)

-- src:4778 | (2) Everyone commits an offence who destroys a document that relates to a request for medical assistance in dying with intent to interfere with
-- src:4779 | (a) another person’s access to medical assistance in dying;
-- src:4780 | (b) the lawful assessment of a request for medical assistance in dying;
-- src:4781 | (c) another person invoking an exemption under any of subsections 227(1) or (2), 241(2) to (5) or 245(2); or
-- src:4782 | (d) the provision by a person of information under section 241.31.
@ref s 241.4(2) (src:4778-4782)
GIVEN `the thing is a document, by s 241.4(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document relates to a request for medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person destroys it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to interfere with another person's access to medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to interfere with the lawful assessment of a request for medical assistance in dying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to interfere with another person invoking an exemption under any of subsections 227(1) or (2), 241(2) to (5) or 245(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to interfere with the provision by a person of information under section 241.31` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241.4(2) the person commits the offence of destroying a document` MEANS
    IF     `the thing is a document, by s 241.4(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the document relates to a request for medical assistance in dying`
       AND `the person destroys it`
       AND (   `the person intends to interfere with another person's access to medical assistance in dying`
            OR `the person intends to interfere with the lawful assessment of a request for medical assistance in dying`
            OR `the person intends to interfere with another person invoking an exemption under any of subsections 227(1) or (2), 241(2) to (5) or 245(2)`
            OR `the person intends to interfere with the provision by a person of information under section 241.31`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone commits an offence who destroys a document that relates to a request for medical assistance in dying with intent to interfere with (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..." (marginal reading M1)

-- src:4784 | (3) Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of
-- src:4785 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:4786 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 241.4(3) (src:4784-4786)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 241.4(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:4785 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
@ref s 241.4(3)(a) (src:4785-4785)
`s 241.4(3)(a) the indictable limb` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:4784 | (3) Everyone who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of
-- src:4785 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:4786 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 241.4(3) (src:4784-4786)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 241.4(3) the punishment` MEANS
    LIST `s 241.4(3)(a) the indictable limb`, `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`
